    <statement><p>Simplify and write the following in exponential notation.</p>
<p>If <m>\left( z^{ \frac{4}{5} } \cdot r^{\frac{4}{7} } \right)^{\frac{2}{3}} = z^{m} \cdot r^n</m> then <m>m =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0001"/>  and  <m>n =</m> <fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\frac{8}{15}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>{\frac{8}{21}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><m>\displaystyle{ \left( z^{ \frac{4}{5} } \cdot r^{\frac{4}{7} } \right)^{\frac{2}{3}} = z^{(4/5)(2/3)} r^{(4/7)(2/3)}=z^{8/15}r^{8/21}}</m></p>
</solution>
